.page set 1 list variables or set the arguments

# SYNOPSIS
*set*
*set* [*--*] [_ARGUMENT_...]

# DESCRIPTION
`set` is a gapsh builtin. Without arguments it prints all the shell variables as `NAME=VALUE`. With arguments it replaces the positional parameters `$1`, `$2` ... by them; leading options (`-e`, `-x` and the like) are accepted and ignored.

# EXAMPLES
    set -- a b c
    echo $# $2
    set -- $(date)

# SEE ALSO
shift(1), export(1)
